A small figure squats beside the fire, knees spread. His skin glistens faintly—smooth, amphibian-dark, flecked with old scars or moss-stains. One hand grips a long walking stick jabbed into the dirt. The other stirs a steaming tin cup set atop a flat rock.
He doesn’t look at you. Just stares into the flames like they’re talking back.
